# No Code Comments

Do **not** add comments to code. This applies to all languages and file types
(inline `//`, block `/* */`, `#`, JSDoc/docstrings, JSX `{/* */}`, etc.).

- Write clear, self-explanatory code with meaningful names instead of comments.
- Do not narrate what code does, restate logic, or add section headers.
- Do not add explanatory comments for the changes you make.
- Leave existing comments untouched unless the task is specifically about them.
- Only exception: add a comment when the user explicitly asks for one.

```ts
// ❌ BAD: commentary added by the agent
// resolve the id to a readable name
const label = names.get(id) ?? id;

// ✅ GOOD: no comment
const label = names.get(id) ?? id;
```
